Notebook[{
Cell["PadicCanonicalize", "ObjectName",ExpressionUUID->"0b3063f1-a11c-4fc6-b3d1-22117d49308d"],

Cell["\<\
PadicCanonicalize[s] rebuilds an exact PadicRational in canonical form, \
minimizing its period and normalizing its valuation. For PadicRationalN it \
normalizes the stored residue without changing the absolute precision e+n or \
reconstructing an exact rational. Lazy objects retain their recipe.\
\>", "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"96565043-1e0c-4be5-9568-bbf556977e8e"],

Cell["\<\
Exact canonicalization reconstructs the rational value, then rebuilds its \
minimal stored expansion, including period reduction and valuation \
normalization.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"56419431-2e92-4cb3-89d1-1fda3ec3a6fd"],

Cell["\<\
Finite-precision canonicalization works directly on the stored residue. It \
preserves absolute precision and distinguishes uncertain zero from exact zero.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"a6c8e1b5-2d09-41d0-b1a6-cbacd994f53b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Needs", "[", "\"\<PadicNumbers`\>\"", 
  "]"}]], "ExampleInitialization",ExpressionUUID->"b17216a5-274e-4d5f-988d-\
fd1e9d872048"],

Cell["Basic Examples", "PrimaryExamplesSection",ExpressionUUID->"4b14fa2a-658f-41fa-9657-553bc00d67cd"],

